# Security review — remove-mempalace-graphify (804f32ff..HEAD)

No HIGH or MEDIUM confidence vulnerabilities found.

Scope reviewed: every file in `git diff --name-only 804f32ff..HEAD`. The
non-markdown delta is almost all deletions: the mempalace hook scripts
(mempalace-checkpoint.sh, mempalace-precompact.sh) and their hooks.json
entries, the vendored mempalace LICENSE, the graphify task (code/graph),
the setup/precommit task, .graphifyignore, the ai/mise.dev.toml mempalace
env, and graphify entries in dprint, taplo, linter, gitleaks, pre-commit and
.gitignore assets. scripts/src/check.ts changes only comments and drops
".graphifyignore" from TOOL_CONFIG_ROOT_FILES. No new code paths, inputs,
subprocess calls, network endpoints or auth logic are introduced; removing
the hooks and the localhost MCP server shrinks attack surface.

Considered and dismissed:
- .gitignore asset no longer ignores graphify-out/, docs/memory/doctor/ and
  docs/memory/runs/, and gitleaks drops its graphify-out/ allowlist path. The
  tool that wrote graphify-out/ is removed, and gitleaks now scans that path
  rather than skipping it. The un-ignored memory paths hold reports, not
  secrets, and data stored on disk is out of scope. Not a vulnerability.
